From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:17:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Fail a request with the error that its backend
 failure calls for

A request that failed in the backend got a "DataError" whatever the
failure was (upstream FIXME in IDBRequest::convert_result). The spec has
no such case: its DataErrors are thrown before a request is made. A put
that finds the disk full should fail with a "QuotaExceededError", a
constraint failure with a "ConstraintError", and an internal storage
failure with an "UnknownError", which is also what its transaction then
aborts with.

convert_result now maps the backend error like the transaction errors
since the P3 review: QuotaExceeded to QuotaExceededError, Constraint to
ConstraintError, Abort to AbortError, anything else (including Unusable,
DbNotFound and StoreNotFound) to UnknownError with a neutral message and
the details in the log. The backend reports a violated constraint of its
tables (SQLITE_CONSTRAINT, RDB_E_SQLITE_CONSTRAINT), which its checks
before writing should prevent, as Constraint rather than DbErr. Stored
values that script can't decode (a postcard failure, a generated key
that can't be injected, a cursor record without its value) are internal
failures too and become UnknownError: the spec's StructuredDeserialize
there can't fail. A databases() call that fails rejects with an
UnknownError, as the spec suggests, rather than "IndexedDB open failed",
and so do open and delete requests that the backend fails (P5 review N5),
as the spec's examples for open step 6 and delete step 11 say, rather
than with an OperationError; the log says "IndexedDB backend failure"
for all of them. idbrequest.rs has one message-less Error use fewer, so
tidy's list of exceptions goes down.

Validation: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits`: 157 passed, 1 skipped (new backend tests, every executor: test_full_database_fails_the_transaction_with_quota_exceeded, a real SQLITE_FULL from max_page_count set inside the open transaction; test_constraint_violation_fails_the_transaction_with_constraint, a real primary key violation from the Faulty executor running an INSERT twice; executor_constraint_violation_keeps_the_transaction checks the Constraint mapping); host SM and QuickJS IndexedDB/ 4,484 of 4,511 each, /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 312 of 312 SM, 310 of 312 QuickJS (interface lists, as before), every result as expected (WPT has no case where the backend fails a request); DAYU200 unit tests: both new tests pass with RDB only and with both backends (RDB only 158 passed, 3 skipped; both 284 passed, 4 skipped at this commit); a temporary hook that limited databases named quota-probe* to 64 pages (not committed, page in the P5.3 notes) gave on host SM: put error QuotaExceededError, the next request AbortError, transaction abort QuotaExceededError, and a later small put on the same connection stored and read back; `./mach test-tidy`: only the known libsqlite3-sys advisory; CI parity at this commit: `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, the crown build (`RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release`), both OHOS flavors with signed HAPs, `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` 1,360 passed, 1 skipped, and `--doc` pass; after the P5 review fix (open and delete failures give UnknownError): host SM release builds, 160 passed, 1 skipped at this commit
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent mapped the request errors, added the backend tests with a real full database and a real constraint violation, and measured the result; the P5 review fix gives open and delete failures UnknownError)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
